Subject: [PATCH] orangepi4pro: cap NPU at 852MHz (shared 0.8V DCDC2 rail)

On the OPi 4 Pro, VDD-NPU sits on the AXP8191 DCDC2 rail, shared with HDMI/DRAM/
UFS/both combo-PHYs and pinned at 0.8V. The NPU 1008/1120MHz OPPs need 0.96V+,
unreachable on this board, so the driver runs 1008MHz undervolted and produces
intermittent silent compute errors (seen via vpm_run golden-compare). Cap at 852MHz
(top 0.8V OPP) in the board dts (not the shared SoC cpu-vf dtsi, so Radxa/other A733
boards are unaffected).

Two changes:
 - Delete opp-1008/opp-1120: this is what actually caps the clock for vipcore (VIPLite
   path), which ignores npu-vf and otherwise selects the top OPP. Validated on HW:
   10000/10000 vipcore golden compares pass at 852MHz.
 - Retarget npu-vf to 852 (0x354): this is galcore's (Unified/OpenVX path) intended OPP.
   In practice galcore currently runs the PLL default (~840MHz -- safe, below the cap)
   because its OPP rate parse is incomplete, so npu-vf is advisory today; it is kept as
   the correct target and to avoid a spurious "CLK FAIL" log once opp-1008 is deleted.
   Harmless to vipcore (which ignores npu-vf).

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-4-pro.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-4-pro.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-4-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-4-pro.dts
@@ -2665,6 +2665,19 @@ &npu {
 	status = "okay";
 };

+/* VDD-NPU shares the 0.8V DCDC2 rail (HDMI/DRAM/UFS/combo-PHYs) so it can't reach the
+ * 0.96V the 1008MHz OPP needs; cap at 852MHz by deleting the 1008/1120 OPPs (this caps
+ * vipcore, which selects the top OPP). npu-vf=852 is galcore's target OPP; galcore today
+ * runs the PLL default (~840MHz, safe, under cap) as its OPP rate-set is incomplete. */
+&npu {
+	npu-vf = <0x354>;	/* 852MHz */
+};
+
+&npu_opp_table {
+	/delete-node/ opp-1008;
+	/delete-node/ opp-1120;
+};
+
 &addr_mgt {
 	compatible     = "allwinner,sunxi-addr_mgt";
 	type_addr_wifi = <0x0>;
